    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0786" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg692"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December 7,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 621.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copies of two dispatches from our
                    consulate-general at Habana presenting the protest of Messrs. Neuhaus, Neumann
                    &amp; Co., of that city, agents of Messrs. S. Hernsheim Bros. &amp; Co., of New
                    Orleans, against the refusal of the authorities in Cuba to allow the exportation
                    of 1,200 bales of tobacco alleged to have been purchased and contracted for
                    prior to the promulgation of General Weyler’s decree of May 16 last forbidding
                    the exportation of tobacco grown in the provinces of Habana and Pinar del
                    Rio.</p>
                <p>You will present this case to the Spanish Government in connection with the
                    tobacco cases previously submitted.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
